/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  variants01_ethanol_water_line -- A UNIT AND A PROPERTY CHECK SELECT THE
  SAME NAMED VARIANT OF THE CASE'S ONE PROPERTY DICTIONARY (DEV.md 4c C398,
  slice (a)).

  ONE CASE, TWO MODES (DEV.md 4c C152): system/flowsheetDict (Process mode,
  choupoSolve, the default) and system/propsDict (Properties & data mode,
  choupoProps) over ONE constant/:
      runCase <case>            Process mode: the pipe, on variant `vogelLaw`
      runCase <case> props      Properties & data mode: the same liquid on
                                the system and on variant `vogelLaw`

  TARGET.  What a reader must be able to answer after running it: which
  liquid viscosity did the pipe use, which law gave it, and where in the
  case was that choice made -- from the printed resolved view, without
  opening a source file.
  SOURCES.  The component records (constant/components/, sealed copies).
  WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM.  That either viscosity law is the better one.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
application   choupoSolve;
description   "Named variants: a pipe and a property check select the same variant of the case's one property dictionary (ethanol-water, liquid viscosity Vogel vs the system's Andrade)";
verbosity     3;

reports
{
    streamTable    { }
    massBalance    { }
    energyBalance  { }
}
